"cmd-1243bd648a1b4701","cmd-a40ac9c2547a43e5","cmd-e2301d6219ab4fbf","cmd-fc3c369407a344f4","cmd-91110919adb743c0","cmd-4bdccb3403d34aac","cmd-5f1f12ae9bdf4ff8","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovery of the mount, LVM state, capacity, payload, OS, and kernel. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate that restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector could not assess failed services because systemd is unavailable on this legacy platform.","The lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum operation and therefore does not independently establish package consistency; however, its result was unchanged from baseline, and no package mutations occurred.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory /etc, so retention of the rc.local backup is inferred from its creation and the absence of a later cleanup command."]}
